WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.120
The Preamble opens with:

2
00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:03.990
We, the people of India.

3
00:00:04.527 --> 00:00:06.146
The authority starts with us.

4
00:00:06.677 --> 00:00:08.674
It calls India a sovereign,

5
00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:11.632
socialist, secular, democratic republic.

6
00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:14.334
But socialist and secular

7
00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:16.914
weren't in the text adopted

8
00:00:16.914 --> 00:00:18.826
on 26 November 1949.

9
00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:21.670
The 42nd Amendment added

10
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:23.053
them in 1976.

11
00:00:23.353 --> 00:00:24.817
Then come four aims:

12
00:00:25.488 --> 00:00:27.221
justice, liberty, equality,

13
00:00:27.221 --> 00:00:28.183
and fraternity.

14
00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:33.061
In Kesavananda Bharati, in 1973,

15
00:00:33.543 --> 00:00:35.100
the Supreme Court treated

16
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.781
the Preamble as part of the

17
00:00:36.781 --> 00:00:37.591
Constitution.

18
00:00:37.913 --> 00:00:40.510
In November 2024, it dismissed

19
00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:43.021
challenges to the 1976 words:

20
00:00:43.349 --> 00:00:44.927
the amending power extends

21
00:00:44.927 --> 00:00:45.898
to the Preamble.

22
00:00:46.238 --> 00:00:47.505
Read it word by word.

23
00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:49.287
Some words have dates.

24
00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:50.149
Your turn.

25
00:00:50.498 --> 00:00:52.656
On which date was the Constitution adopted?
